Z||000001||p4n1c||05-09-2001||08:20 AM||||After getting food poisoning from that god foresaken pizza chain I wouldn't want to eat anything they created.<P>Their garlic crap is more than likely mayo, crushed garlic cloves and a bit of spit from each employee.<P>------------------<BR>-=-=-=[ p4n1c ]=-=-=-<BR>1988 Olds Cutlass Supreme International||||reg||1
Z||000002||JSocha||05-09-2001||09:11 AM||||What do you need help on?<P>Do you want to make the sauce from scratch?  <BR>Pre-fabbed sauce with some mods?<P>I can dig through some of my recipes for a garlic sauce that may just work on Pizza...as I have never used it that way (mostly on Pasta).  I may have to modify one of my recipes a tish to thicken it for Pizza.<P>I'll work on emailing you with possibly several this evening and after I mow my yard (Central Daylight Time).<P>------------------<BR>    <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/jsocha.jpg"> ||||reg||1
Z||000003||JSocha||05-09-2001||10:05 AM||||PIZZA SAUCE (Recipe #1)<P>2.....Tblsp Bella olive oil <BR>......(use the best olive oil...and in this case do not use Extra Virgin Olive Oil as you will get a funny taste to the sauce...yuck...tried it twice with homemade Pasta Sauce...regular works better!)<P>1.....Garlic clove, crushed<BR>......(or more depending on your love of and for garlic...if your trying to avoid Vampires at Halloween, the more the better!)<P>1.....28 Oz can tomato puree<P>1.....Tsp dried marjoram<P>1.....Tsp dried basil<P>Salt and pepper (I like to use fresh ground), to your individual liking<P>Now, over medium heat, heat the olive oil in a saucepan until it is hot (not to the point where it is setting off your smoke detector!). <P>Add all the remaining ingredients, stir well, cover and bring to a boil. <P>Uncover, stir, lower the heat and allow it to simmer for at least 30 minutes or until it reduces and thickins.<P>Let cool.<P>You should get about 2 3/4 to 3 cups (typically 3)<P>Had to run home for the company's laptop and my digital camera so I grabbed this recipe out of my collection.<BR>==================================<BR>TOMATO PIZZA SAUCE (Recipe #2)<P>1   tblsp olive oil (Bella)<BR>1   large garlic clove, minced <BR>1/4 tsp freshly ground pepper<BR> <BR>1   28 Oz can Italian plum tomatoes including the juice <P>In a large heavy saucepan over moderately low heat, cook the garlic and pepper in the olive oil, stirring for about 2 minutes or until the mixture is fragrant.<P>Add the tomatoes, squashing them in your hand, with the juice, bring the mixture to a boil, and cook it over moderately low heat, stirring occasionally, for 20 to 30 minutes, or until the sauce is thickened and reduced to approximately 2 cups. <P>Season the sauce with salt. <P>Referigerate as the sauce will keep, if covered and chilled for about 1 week and makes about 2 cups. <P>Let me know how it turns out!<BR>------------------<BR>       <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/jsocha.jpg"> <p>[This message has been edited by JSocha (edited 05-09-2001).]||||reg||1
